  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist \"Okafor CRC 2026\" (RBC-QM-02) is done. All 5 members are in the population (aged 46–75 at the end of 2026). 4 have an open gap and now have a FIT kit order and an outreach message. 1 is excluded.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0011), patient messaged (comm-t0012) | I first classed her as excluded (frailty plus donepezil). Then Dr. Lin's message arrived: the frailty entry (cond-00189) belonged to another patient and is now entered in error. Without frailty that exclusion fails, so I revised the decision. Nothing had been ordered or sent before, so nothing needed undoing. No other exclusion, and no qualifying screening on record. Note doc-t0013 documents this. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice care during 2026: the episode ran 06/16/2026–08/21/2026 and is now finished (eoc-00002, hospice discharge summary doc-00402). Ending it to join a clinical trial does not cancel the exclusion. No order and no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (52) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0001), patient messaged (comm-t0004) | A correction arrived during review: the FIT (obs-01732) was collected 12/31/2025, not 01/05/2026 (that was the lab's receipt date). Collection falls outside 2026, so it doesn't count. No other screening on record and no exclusions. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0002), patient messaged (comm-t0005) | The 06/2024 stool DNA test (obs-01871) was withdrawn by the lab because the specimen belonged to another patient. It is now entered in error (lab notice doc-00401). The 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003, still active) was never done, and an order doesn't count. No exclusions. |\n| pt-0073 Marisol Quintero (58) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0003), patient messaged (comm-t0006) | The 01/2026 FIT report (obs-73001) was cancelled. The lab re-issued it as obs-05001 with a collection date of 12/28/2025, which is outside 2026 (lab notice doc-00403). No other screening on record and no exclusions. |\n\n- **Orders and messages:** each FIT order runs 10/23/2026–12/31/2026. None of these patients had an active FIT order. Each message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect and return it, with no claims about past results.\n- **New items while I worked:** five arrived (inbox-a0001 to a0005), one for each patient above. I reviewed and closed each one with a comment.\n- **Left for you:** your other inbox items (results and refill requests) have nothing to do with this worklist, and I didn't touch them.",
